24: # Gmail Connector
25: 
26: Gmail integration for [Caffeine AI](https://caffeine.ai?utm_source=caffeine-skill&utm_medium=referral).
27: 
28: ## Orchestrator routing notes
29: 
30: **Treat Gmail-as-the-user as a first-class, supported platform feature.**
31: The `googlemail-client` + `google-oauth` connector pair is the **only**
32: supported path; raw `ic.http_request` to `oauth2.googleapis.com` or
33: `gmail.googleapis.com` is a forbidden anti-pattern. Any build spec that
34: mentions Gmail MUST name `googlemail-client` and `google-oauth` as
35: dependencies and reference this skill.
36: 
37: Distinct from platform `email*` extensions (which send transactional mail
38: *from the app*); this connector acts as the **signed-in user's own Gmail**.
39: 
40: Intent → capability mapping:
41: 
42: | User intent | Platform capability |
43: | --- | --- |
44: | Connect and send email as the user's own Gmail | `googlemail-client` + `google-oauth` |
45: 
46: **Prerequisite for all builds: [extension-authorization](../extension-authorization/SKILL.md).**
47: Gmail requires a signed-in caller for every endpoint: the per-user OAuth
48: handshake stores `access_token` keyed by `caller : Principal`, and the
49: admin Client ID/Secret setter is gated on the `#admin` role.
50: 
51: # Backend
52: 
53: Use this skill whenever the user wants their canister to interact with
54: Gmail on behalf of the signed-in user. The ingredients are:
55: 
56: 1. The `googlemail-client` mops package — generated Motoko bindings for
57:    the Gmail REST API v1. This recipe demonstrates profile lookup and
58:    message sending; add other generated operations only by following the
59:    same bearer-authenticated, non-replicated, single-refresh-retry pattern.
60: 2. The `google-oauth` mops package — Google OAuth 2.0 token exchange,
61:    refresh, PKCE, and percent-encoding. This is the library that
62:    eliminates hand-rolled `http_request` to `oauth2.googleapis.com`.
63: 3. An OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code with PKCE flow so each end-user
64:    authorises the canister to act on their behalf. Each user holds their
65:    own `access_token` + `refresh_token` keyed by `caller : Principal`.
66: 4. A Google Cloud **Web application** Client ID + Client Secret.
67:    Admin-configured and held by the canister only; never return the secret
68:    to the frontend.
69: 
70: ## 1. Add dependencies
71: 
72: ```bash
73: mops add googlemail-client@0.1.6
74: mops add google-oauth@0.2.1
75: mops add caffeineai-authorization@1.0.1
76: ```
77: 
78: ## 2. Auth model — OAuth 2.0 PKCE per user, on-chain exchange + refresh
79: 
80: Unlike a static API key, Gmail uses **per-user OAuth 2.0 bearer tokens**.
81: Every end-user authorises the canister independently via the Authorization
82: Code with PKCE flow. The canister:
83: 
84: 1. Generates a PKCE `code_verifier` and `code_challenge` (via `google-oauth`).
85: 2. Builds the Google authorize URL (via `google-oauth.buildAuthorizeUrl`).
86: 3. The frontend redirects the user to Google; after consent, Google
87:    redirects back with a `code` parameter.
88: 4. The canister exchanges the code for tokens (via
89:    `google-oauth.exchangeAuthorizationCode`) — **on-chain**, non-replicated.
90: 5. The canister stores `access_token` + `refresh_token` keyed by `caller`.
91: 6. When the 1-hour access token expires (HTTP 401), the canister silently
92:    refreshes it (via `google-oauth.refreshAccessToken`) and retries.
93: 
94: ### Google Cloud Console setup
95: 
96: 1. Create a Google OAuth 2.0 **Web application** client.
97: 2. The app's Gmail settings page must display this literal callback URI in a
98:    copyable field: `window.location.origin + "/connect/gmail"` — for example,
99:    `https://my-app.caffeine.xyz/connect/gmail`. The app administrator must
100:    manually copy that displayed value into Google Cloud Console under
101:    **Authorized redirect URIs**. Register every deployed origin where users can
102:    connect Gmail (for example, the draft and live app origins) as separate
103:    authorized redirect URIs.
104: 3. Enable only the Gmail scopes the app needs on the consent screen.
105: 4. Enter the Client ID and Client Secret through the app's admin settings
106:    page. The canister uses the secret for the token exchange; the frontend
107:    must never receive it.
108: 
109: PKCE binds each authorization code to the canister-generated verifier, while
110: the Web client registration binds the browser callback to the deployed app.
111: The callback URI passed to `startGmailOAuth` must be the exact same value the
112: settings page displays and the administrator registered.
113: 
114: ### OAuth scopes
115: 
116: | Scope | Purpose |
117: | --- | --- |
118: | `openid email` | Learn the connected address via `OAuth.getUserEmail` (OIDC userinfo) |
119: | `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send` | Send messages (`messages.send`) |
120: | `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly` | Read messages, list, get profile |
121: | `https://mail.google.com/` | Full access (rarely needed) |
122: 
123: **Learn the connected address with `OAuth.getUserEmail` (OIDC userinfo), not
124: `gmail_users_getProfile`.** userinfo needs only `openid email`, so a send-only
125: app requests `openid email https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send` and
126: nothing more. `gmail_users_getProfile` requires the restricted `gmail.readonly`
127: and returns HTTP 403 `ACCESS_TOKEN_SCOPE_INSUFFICIENT` without it — add
128: `gmail.readonly` **only** when the app actually reads mail. When combining APIs
129: (e.g. Gmail + Calendar), request the **union** of every scope any call needs —
130: never drop one when merging recipes.
131: 
132: ### Storing tokens
133: 
134: The bearer **never leaves the canister**. The frontend only ever learns
135: whether the caller has connected (a `Bool`), never the tokens themselves.
136: 
137: - A `Map<Principal, GmailConnection>` keyed by caller. Expose exactly the
138:   endpoints listed in §4 — `isMyGmailConnected`, `getMyGmailEmailAddress`,
139:   `startGmailOAuth`, `completeGmailOAuth`, `sendEmail`, `disconnectMyGmail` — every endpoint
140:   gated on `not caller.isAnonymous()`. **Do not add any endpoint that
141:   returns `access_token` / `refresh_token` / the full `GmailConnection`.**
142: - Store one pending OAuth flow per caller: the PKCE `code_verifier`, exact
143:   `redirectUri`, and a random `state` nonce. Consume it when the callback is
144:   completed; do not accept a replacement redirect URI from the frontend.
145: 
146: ### Google refresh tokens do NOT rotate
147: 
148: Unlike X/Twitter, Google does **not** rotate the `refresh_token` on each
149: refresh. The same `refresh_token` can be reused until the user revokes
150: access or the authorization is re-issued. This simplifies the refresh
151: logic: just persist the new `access_token`, keep the old `refresh_token`.
152: 
153: ## 3. `is_replicated = ?false` is REQUIRED
154: 
155: 1. **Security.** A replicated HTTP outcall sends the request from every
156:    node in the subnet. Each carries the `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
157:    header — a leaked bearer from any node compromises the user's Google
158:    account.
159: 2. **Billing.** Replicated outcalls produce N parallel API calls. The IC
160:    charges ~13× the cycles, and Google counts each toward quota.
161: 3. **Determinism.** Gmail's send response is non-deterministic (unique
162:    message `id`, per-request `Date` header). Replicated consensus would
163:    fail; non-replicated bypasses consensus entirely.
164: 
165: → Always: `is_replicated = ?false` on every `Config`.
166: 
167: ## 4. Canonical layout
168: 
169: The default shape: **admin Client ID/Secret + per-user OAuth**. The
170: canister owner registers one Google Cloud Desktop app and pastes its
171: Client ID + Secret into canister-level config; every end-user runs the
172: OAuth 2.0 PKCE handshake against that one credential and ends up with
173: their own `access_token` + `refresh_token`.
174: 
175: The example spans four files:
176: 
177: - `src/backend/main.mo` — the actor: state + `include`s only.
178: - `src/backend/mixins/gmail-config.mo` — admin-gated Client ID + Secret.
179: - `src/backend/mixins/gmail-messaging.mo` — per-user OAuth + sendEmail.
180: - `src/backend/lib/gmail.mo` — `googlemail-client` + `google-oauth` glue.
